**Best practice:** Test your Verilog modules and testbenches before committing completed changes.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Before starting work:
git pull --rebase origin main
Whenever you make changes to your Verilog files, use:
    git status
    git add .
    git commit -m "Describe your changes"
    git push
For example, after implementing your next processor module:
    git add rtl/alu.v tb/tb_alu.v
    git commit -m "Improve ALU implementation and tests"
    git pull --rebase origin main
    git push

My recommendation: For our RISC-V project, we'll follow this simple rule:
Pull → Code → Test → Commit → Push